  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Implemented and exercised a deterministic complex-cubic LMFDB corpus generator, strict offline validator, and pinned-label replay. The frozen corpus has 12 named controls, 1,000 tune records (50 in every one of 20 discriminant/class-group cells), and 400 holdout records (the next 20 in every cell). A committed 47 KB content-addressed manifest contains no records and binds the normalized SQL, the canonical 1,815-label exposure set and derivation, source metadata, counts, logical hashes, gzip hashes, release URLs, and CC-BY-SA-4.0 attribution. Real public-LMFDB generation and independent pinned-label replay both returned exactly 1,412 records with source digest c94049d975c64d05aec973191892a3a3f580d4732a1a8c7aada2f94b43549144. Network-free synthetic tests cover the exact counts, every rank, ordering, metadata, deterministic compression, canonical serialization, corruption, exposure leakage, manifest identity, and replay-without-resampling contract.",
    "risks": [
      "The two content-addressed gzip assets are intentionally untracked at /tmp/complex-cubic-frontier-v1-final and must be uploaded without renaming before the manifest release URLs resolve.",
      "The no-install lane omits the optional FLINT addon. pnpm test:compiler passes after provisioning the same-HEAD ignored addon artifacts from the root checkout; pnpm build passes cleanly with optional native adapters absent.",
      "LMFDB is a mutable external source. The replay command deliberately fails closed if a pinned record changes or disappears; it never resamples a replacement."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Upload the exact survey and holdout gzip files from /tmp/complex-cubic-frontier-v1-final to GitHub release optimization-corpus-complex-cubic-v1.",
      "Use only the survey asset during tuning; open the holdout asset only after freezing the candidate and intervention.",
      "Run the corpus check command after downloading the release assets and preserve the committed manifest with benchmark evidence."
    ]
  }
